WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.732
Welcome to Module 2 of The
Daily Checks on One Dashboard:

2
00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:07.013
reading it, deploying it,
and keeping the evidence.

3
00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:09.701
A dashboard's most
dangerous state isn't red:

4
00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.538
it's green over a source
that stopped arriving.

5
00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:17.239
In this module you read the workbook the
way an operator should, telemetry first;

6
00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:20.729
deploy it the way a change should
go, previewed and approved;

7
00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:23.650
and keep the evidence the
way an assessor needs it.

8
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.938
About forty minutes, plus a lab.

9
00:00:25.938 --> 00:00:28.930
The module has been reviewed and approved.

10
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:37.806
By the end of this module you'll be able
to read each tab as attention, clear,

11
00:00:37.806 --> 00:00:43.359
stale, no data or link-out; explain why an
empty queue over a stale source is stale;

12
00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:48.571
run the reachability check and read
its result; deploy by an approved hash,

13
00:00:48.571 --> 00:00:52.180
and roll back; and say what
is, and isn't, evidence.

14
00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:58.093
Unit 1: reading the workbook.

15
00:00:58.093 --> 00:01:02.236
Telemetry completeness comes
first, because every other tab

16
00:01:02.236 --> 00:01:06.217
depends on its sources: a dark
source is a high-severity task.

17
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:10.539
Then each tab in turn, and each
row that needs work becomes,

18
00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:13.205
or is matched to, a task with an owner.

19
00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:17.105
Entra Health and the I T S M
queue are worked where they live.

20
00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:22.092
The workbook never closes a task, pages
anyone, or proves a check happened.

21
00:01:22.092 --> 00:01:27.142
And the rule: an empty queue over a
stale source reads stale, never clear.

22
00:01:27.142 --> 00:01:31.254
A missed probe shows yesterday's
verdict, so its tab is stale too.

23
00:01:31.254 --> 00:01:35.747
A synchronization server or domain
controller that stops sending

24
00:01:35.747 --> 00:01:39.517
isn't an empty list: it's a row
with an old heartbeat, flagged.

25
00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:45.410
And the replication probe needs Enterprise
Admins or equivalent to read replication,

26
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.550
so it runs only on a Tier
0 host, or not at all.

27
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.038
Unit 2: deploying it.

28
00:01:54.038 --> 00:01:56.550
What-if previews the
change and makes none,

29
00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.426
and it needs the same deployment
rights as the deployment itself.

30
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:03.370
The plan's hash is what
a second person approves,

31
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:07.750
and the kit deploys nothing else; it
refuses any plan that would delete.

32
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:10.941
The deployer holds Workbook
Contributor and deployment

33
00:02:10.941 --> 00:02:13.600
rights on the resource
group only, for the window.

34
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.125
Rollback is a redeploy of
the previous approved plan,

35
00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:20.610
or a delete that removes
a view and nothing else.

36
00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.422
Unit 3: the evidence.

37
00:02:26.422 --> 00:02:31.039
The kit records the validation, the
preflight, the plan, the deployment,

38
00:02:31.039 --> 00:02:34.064
the reachability check
and the rollback plan,

39
00:02:34.064 --> 00:02:37.885
each hashed and chained, with
its controls and indicators.

40
00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:42.685
It refuses a render, with the words:
a rendered view is not evidence.

41
00:02:42.685 --> 00:02:45.485
A screenshot of a tab
isn't evidence either.

42
00:02:45.485 --> 00:02:49.330
And at the go or no-go,
only live records count.

43
00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.005
Who does what?

44
00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:59.330
Operators read telemetry first, then
their family's tabs, and open the tasks.

45
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:03.392
Security operations plans,
deploys and checks reachability.

46
00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:06.831
A second person approves the
plan's hash in the change record.

47
00:03:06.831 --> 00:03:11.942
And the security officer keeps the evidence
folder, never a render or a screenshot.

48
00:03:11.942 --> 00:03:15.687
The plan and what-if support change
control and impact analysis;

49
00:03:15.687 --> 00:03:19.784
the reachability record supports
continuous and system monitoring;

50
00:03:19.784 --> 00:03:23.881
and the chained records support the
protection of audit information.

51
00:03:23.881 --> 00:03:25.750
The assessor decides.

52
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.763
Lab 1 is in the developer workbook's
Chapter 3, on a laptop with no tenant.

53
00:03:34.763 --> 00:03:37.722
You render the morning
of November sixteenth,

54
00:03:37.722 --> 00:03:41.228
when the Entra diagnostic
setting stopped overnight,

55
00:03:41.228 --> 00:03:44.811
the probe didn't run and a
domain controller went silent:

56
00:03:44.811 --> 00:03:48.472
four telemetry rows flagged;
sync, risk, emergency access,

57
00:03:48.472 --> 00:03:52.601
grants and admin changes all stale;
and the Active Directory tab,

58
00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:56.262
whose sources are fresh,
flagging the silent controller.

59
00:03:56.262 --> 00:03:59.398
Then you render the next
morning, run the replication

60
00:03:59.398 --> 00:04:02.962
probe on a saved replication
report, and check reachability.

61
00:04:02.962 --> 00:04:07.720
And when you try to record the first
render as evidence, the kit refuses.

62
00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.618
Lab 2 runs the reachability check
against a test workspace, then,

63
00:04:15.618 --> 00:04:20.080
with a change record, the runbook's
first stage in a test subscription:

64
00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.132
never production, and the
authors haven't run it.

65
00:04:23.132 --> 00:04:24.258
Two questions.

66
00:04:24.258 --> 00:04:26.861
On the morning the sign-in logs stopped,

67
00:04:26.861 --> 00:04:29.870
the risk tab returns no
rows: what does it show?

68
00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.645
Stale, because its source is
past its sixty-minute limit.

69
00:04:33.645 --> 00:04:36.757
And when the what-if shows a
delete, what does the kit do?

70
00:04:36.757 --> 00:04:40.670
It refuses the plan: the workbook
deployment never deletes.

71
00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:45.370
In summary: you read the workbook
telemetry first, deployed it previewed and

72
00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:50.280
approved by hash, and kept the checks'
records as the evidence, never the picture.
